      "difficulty": "application",
      "stem": "Make r the subject of: V = (4/3)pi*r^3",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "r = cube root of (3V / (4*pi))" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "r = cube root of (4V / (3*pi))" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "r = 3V / (4*pi)" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "r = sqrt(3V / (4*pi))" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "a",
      "explanation": "V = (4/3)pi*r^3. Multiply by 3: 3V = 4*pi*r^3. Divide by 4*pi: r^3 = 3V/(4*pi). Cube root: r = cube root of (3V/(4*pi))."
    },
